{"availability":"available","full":"anulum/sc-neurocore","name":"sc-neurocore","description":"Universal Stochastic Computing Framework for Neuromorphic Hardware — Rust SIMD engine, Python simulation, Verilog RTL, HDC/VSA, SCPN integration","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":15,"forks":0,"created":"2026-02-10T11:52:34Z","updated":"2026-10-11T20:25:48Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://anulum.github.io/sc-neurocore/","topics":["edge-ai","fpga","hyper-dimensional-computing","neuromorphic","neuromorphic-computing","petri-nets","pyo3","quantum","rust","simd","snn","spiking-neural-networks","stochastic-computing","verilog"],"demo":"https://anulum.github.io/sc-neurocore/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:16.759Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:16.759Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:28:16.759Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:57.878Z","stars":15,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:28:16.759Z","stars":15,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python","Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Stochastic computing and neuromorphic hardware co-design toolkit","SC-NeuroCore is a research-to-hardware software stack for designing spiking and stochastic neural systems, validating their numerical behaviour, and moving selected models toward FPGA, ASIC, and embedded neuromorphic deployment. It combines a Python public API, an optional Rust acceleration engine, SystemVerilog generation paths, benchmark evidence, and polyglot research mirrors for selected kernels.","It is useful when a team needs to answer practical questions such as:"],"features":["Can a stochastic bitstream representation approximate this neural computation within a bounded error budget?","Which neuron, synapse, encoder, or network path is numerically appropriate for a target workload?","Can a model be converted into auditable hardware artefacts rather than remaining only a Python simulation?","Which evidence is available